I was complaining not too long ago about monsters shooting down long 
dark corridors at invisible players, and so on.  This patch fixes that
behavior.  It is a re-write of the routine set_apparxy() from monmove.c.
This is the routine the monsters use to figure out where you are at.
I've re-written it for more consistent and logical behavior.  Monsters
can use sight, hearing and smell to locate you, and they may place you
exactly or have only a general idea of your location.  Pets track you
through a psychic connection, and high level monster have a chance to
just know where you are - so keep moving!

This also includes a new file, los.c, which contains very efficient
line-of-sight code from rec.games.programmer.  Nethack has about 27
different functions that do some version of los or distance.  The dev
team might want to consider using the code in los.c to replace some of
those functions.

This has been more or less tested, but might still have bugs.  In
particular, I don't know how it will affect the lower levels/end game,
since I rarely get down there :-(.  It does make the earlier levels 
somewhat easier, but the effect is minimal.  On the plus side, it gives
the player some tactical ability - you can actually "lose" a monster 
if you can open up a lead on him.

There's also a small change to mthrowu to fix the problem with monsters
peppering you with missiles when they don't know where you are.  I've
also included a test that keeps monsters from shooting other monsters
accidently, if HARD is defined.

Enjoy.

						-- Scott Turner

